The VOC also became involved in expensive political conflicts in Java. The Third Javanese War of Succession began in 1746 after opposition to Dutch interference in local political affairs. The conflict would continue beyond the proposed investment period, demonstrating the company's willingness to become involved in regional power struggles to protect its interests.
